# Paths this repository may track. check_tracked_paths.py fails when a
# tracked file matches no line here, and when a line here matches no
# tracked file (so a stale line cannot quietly widen what is allowed).
#
# `*` and `?` stay within one directory and also match dotfiles, `**/`
# spans any depth, and `{a,b}` is expanded before matching; every
# alternative must match a tracked file.
# Prefer a place and a file type over a single file; name a single file
# only when it is the one file of its kind in that place.
#
# Adding a line is a decision about what may be published: TPM installs
# ccm by cloning this repository, so every tracked file is shipped.

# --- Repository root --------------------------------------------------------
.gitignore
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
LICENSE
README.md
README.ja.md
ccm
ccm.tmux
ccm.tmux.conf

# --- Repository tooling -----------------------------------------------------
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.md
.github/workflows/ci.yml
scripts/*.py
scripts/tracked_paths.allow

# --- Plugin -----------------------------------------------------------------
lib/*.{py,sh}
hooks/*.sh
completions/_ccm

# --- Documentation ----------------------------------------------------------
docs/*.md
assets/*.{png,svg}

# --- Tests ------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/*.{py,bats}
tests/helpers/*.bash
tests/helpers/sidekick_option_probe.py
tests/fixtures/*.json
tests/fixtures/docs/*.json
tests/fixtures/snapshot/*.py
tests/fixtures/snapshot/v1-implementation.txt
tests/fixtures/tmux_guard/*.fixture
tests/fixtures/traces/*.events.jsonl
